\cf1\b\fs32 New Features \fs24 (since 1.30)\cf0\b0\fs20\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720\fs24 On-board and Host DMA optimization for higher frame rate support.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx1440\f1\'b7\fs20\tab\f0\fs24 Serial port speed support up to 921600 baud.\par
\f1\'b7\fs20\tab\f0\fs24 Support for physical LVAL invalid of 2 pixel minimum. Original design needed a minimum of 4 pixels.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx1440 Shaft encoder enhancements: support for parameters CORACQ_PRM_SHAFT_ENCODER_DIRECTION, CORACQ_PRM_LINE_TRIGGER_AUTO_DELAY and ACQ events: Shaft encoder reverse count overflow, Line trigger too fast and External line trigger too slow. \cf2\f2\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx1440\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\li720\cf0\f0\fs20\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\cf1\b\fs32 Fixes \fs24 (since 1.30)\ul\fs32\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx180\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs24 Multi-thread/multi-board initialization of ACQ/XFER.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible missing 1st frame of a sequence when an Abort is done before acquiring.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}ACQ event not received by Sapera Monitor if application does not register at least one ACQ event.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible acquisition pass the virtual end of frame in RGB line scan mode.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Increased length of auto-generated board sync signal when option 'To Board Sync' is selected on the Master board. Slave boards could miss pulses.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible board not being able to re-train after a board reset.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sb40\sa20\tx360\tx720 When grabbing with a  base camera using a Medium or Full configuration, the 2nd unused camera input could affect the acquired images.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Optimized XferSelect and XferAppend functions which were taking exponential times.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}FFC with dual channel cameras.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720 When using a dual camera configuration, possibility of events being turned off when creating an Xfer handle on one camera while grabbing with the other one.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}When grabbing from base or medium camera configuration, possible interference from unused 2nd and/or 3rd CameraLink chip output causing acquired image to be a flat grey image.  \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible Data Overflow using Dual FFC FPGA and segmented tap configuration.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible tap de-synchronization when acquiring variable frame length images with segmented tap configuration.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible buffer incomplete of acquired images in segmented tap configuration with segments having right-to-left direction.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Improved FPGA memory interfacing in order to better support a wider range memory manufacturer.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx720\cf1\fs32\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\sl240\slmult0\b Backward Compatibility\b0\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult0\tx720\cf2\f1\fs20\'b7\tab\f0\fs24 Compatible with Sapera LT version 5.20 and later (XP), 6.02 and later (Windows Vista & Windows 7).\par
\f1\fs20\'b7\tab\f0\fs24 For Wow64 driver under 64-bit OS,  compatible with Sapera LT version \cf0 7.11.02.1052\cf2\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li720\sl240\slmult0\tx720\fs20\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\cf1\b\fs32 Notes\cf0\b0\fs20\par
\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720\fs24 Cropping width must be a multiple of 16 pixels.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Hactive must be a multiple of 16 pixels/taps with multi-segmented tap cameras.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Serial ports are only available once a Sapera application has started/executed. This will be the case in most instances as Device Manager runs on every bootup. \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}4 taps of 8 bits with alternated taps and Camera Link configuration "two bases" is not supported.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}External Trigger Acquisition Callback \par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li1440\tx720 Line scan: edge and level trigger\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Area scan: edge trigger only\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720 The LUT must not be change/set while grabbing.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Vertical flip, Horizontal flip and cropping is not supported for 10 taps camera.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Horizontal flip is not support for dual channel camera and for 2 alternated taps 10 or 12 bits camera.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}For 10 taps camera, to maximize the bandwidth, do not crop horizontally and use a multiple of 8 lines.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}In variable frame length, the external trigger must be inactive for at least one line.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Monochrome camera with 8 taps alternated and color camera with 2 taps alternated are not supported.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}When a software trigger is used the parameter CORACQ_PRM_EXT_TRIGGER_DELAY has no effect.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}To optimize transfer bandwidth, parallel taps of 8 and 10 taps are automatically merged if the following conditions are met\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li1440\tx720 No horizontal or vertical flipping is requested\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}All tap directions are from top to bottom\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}No horizontal cropping of incoming image is requested\line\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li720\tx720\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li1440\tx720 If the number of vertical lines to acquire is not a multiple of the number of lines to merge, no merging will be done.\line\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li720\tx720 For line length of 2K and less, line merging will be done on 2, 4 or 8 lines depending on the line length in pixels.\par
\tab 0 - 800 : 4 lines\line\tab 801 - 1024 : 2 lines\line\tab 1025 - 2048 : 8 lines \par
\line Line length multiple of 2K: No merging.\line For line length > 2K, number of lines merged = 2048 / (Line Length % 2048), max of 8 lines. If number of vertical lines to acquire is not a\line multiple of the number of lines to merge, the driver will try to merge less lines.\line       \par
\pard\nowidctlpar\fi-720\li1440\tx720 Line merging imposes constraint on the number of vertical lines that must be a multiple of the number of lines merged. This can be an issue when acquiring variable frame length images. If transfer bandwidth is not an issue, the CORXFER_PRM_LINE_MERGING can be used to turn off the automatic line merging of parallel taps of 8 and 10 taps.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720 In 3-tap parallel configuration, the DataValid signal is always active, and cannot be de-activated. \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}The buffer parameter CORBUFFER_PRM_SPACE_USED is updated only if the transfer event 'End of Frame' is registered.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}The buffer state CORBUFFER_VAL_STATE_OVERFLOW is set only if the transfer event 'End of Frame' is registered.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}The external frame trigger (in linescan) when set to acquire on a level high or low, will only start acquisition when an edge, rising or falling respectively, is detected.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}When acquiring from 2 bayer sources simultaneously, it is recommended to create 3 or more internal buffers per input in order to avoid losing frames. \line Also, note that there is only one bayer to RGB converter on the board, so images are converted in a serial fashion.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sb40\sa20\tx360\tx720 Removed HS80 specific firmware ("\b\f3\fs20 One Full Camera Link Input with Flat Field Correction\b0  (FFC), optimized for use with the Teledyne DALSA HS-80 camera.\f0\fs24 "). The optimization has been integrated\line into the standard Full FPGA. \par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx1440 Dual Bayer firmware supports serial port speed up to 115200 baud and supports a minimum of 4 pixels for the physical LVAL.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Flat-Line correction is not supported with 10-tap FPGA.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\ul\b\par
