\cf1\b\fs32 New Features\cf0\b0\fs20\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720\fs24 Windows 7 support.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Supports Sapera Monitor tool\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Added optimized CameraLink Full Firmware with Flatfield correction, to support DALSA's HS-80 camera.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Support for 3-tap parallel, 8-bit monochrome (Dual board).\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}10-tap FPGA now supports any line width multiple of 10 pixels instead of 80 pixels.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Added support for installation switch /cr to require a reboot of the PC when a reset of the board is requested. This switch is useful on a minority of systems that generate a BSOD when the board is reset.\cf2\par
\cf0{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Support for new Xfer parameter CORXFER_PRM_LINE_MERGING to control automatic or turning off merging of lines to optimize transfer bandwidth.\cf2\par
\cf0{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Support for 'Shaft Encoder' time base for time stamping buffers.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Medium and Full Bayer cameras.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Acquiring Infinite number of frames upon receiving one external trigger.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}2 channels with timeslot 2 cameras.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Support for Basler Sprint Camera using Bayer Method 6.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}100 nsec resolution for internal line trigger.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}100 msec time base for timers, permitting integration of over 70 minutes.\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlcont\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\li720\fs20\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlcont\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\cf1\b\fs32 Fixes\ul\par
\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx180\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs24 Camera with 4 taps of 16-bits per pixel.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Linescan acquisition into host buffers that are bigger than 1/2 the internal on-board memory.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Bayer decoding of 2 cameras of 12-bits per pixel.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Timestamp source for the 2nd camera was always using the usec timestamp independently of the one selected by user\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}PoCL and camera DALSA HCL, the clock of the camera stopped for less than 100ms causing the power to be removed.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Starting Device Manager at the same time as an Application caused Device Manager saying 'randomly' that the Firmware needs an update.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Acquisition of camera CV-M8CL was not working: the FVAL falling edge is 1 pixel clock before the LVAL falling edge.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Time integration of a vertically cropped image was not working.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Buffer 'overflow' state when XferDesc is not used with XferAppend. \par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Buffer 'overflow' state when line merging is active.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}External Trigger Delay value was taken into account even if the external trigger was disabled.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Support for 12/14/16 bits per pixel, dual channel camera.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Grabbing into host image buffers that are bigger than the on-board memory.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Possible corrupted image when grabbing dual RGB or dual Bayer cameras with big image size.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}FFC with lines > 4KB\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Horizontal flipping of images for multi-segemented taps.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Variable frame length trigger shorter than time it takes to fill host buffer, host buffer could still be filled when using segmented taps.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}GIO callbacks would only be generated on falling edges even if user requested rising edges.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Host buffers > 4 GB in size.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Host buffers crossing 4GB boundaries would generate a black line on this boundary.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}PCIe training issues in some computers.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Optimized connection/disconnection time when using large amount of host buffers.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Increased length of auto-generated board sync signal. Slave boards could miss pulses.\par
\pard\nowidctlpar\tx720\cf1\fs32\par
